37f1a672-cca3-49b4-9190-aeb5af956503	ECB SAFE survey: lending conditions for euro area firms tightened	The ECB's Survey on the Access to Finance of Enterprises reports that lending conditions for firms have tightened.	The European Central Bank published its latest Survey on the Access to Finance of Enterprises (SAFE). It indicates that lending conditions faced by firms tightened. The release headline gives no figures.\n\nTighter credit conditions could weigh on euro area business investment and hiring, which would likely dampen growth momentum. If that persists, it could add to the case for a more accommodative ECB stance. That could push euro area yields lower and weigh on the euro, with possible pressure on EURUSD.\n\nThe effects on global markets are likely modest. However, a softer euro could lend mild support to the US dollar index.\n\nSource: [ECB - European Central Bank](https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261026~bde7b6d11a.en.html)	2026-10-26 09:00:00+00	economy	{EURUSD,DXY}	\N	ECB - European Central Bank	https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261026~bde7b6d11a.en.html	33bacda3-c4d5-47b8-8ec4-e885bbd5157f	2026-10-29 20:05:11.048951+00
