ab70070f-a2d2-4a42-9350-202c62e8ef83	ECB publishes Consumer Expectations Survey results for September 2026	The European Central Bank released the results of its Consumer Expectations Survey for September 2026.	The European Central Bank (ECB) has published the results of its Consumer Expectations Survey for September 2026. The release did not include specific figures in the information provided.\n\nThe survey tracks euro area consumers' expectations, including views on inflation, which the ECB watches closely when setting monetary policy. Shifts in consumer inflation expectations could influence market pricing of future ECB rate decisions. That in turn could affect euro area yields and the euro's exchange rate, for example against the US dollar. The direction of any impact depends on the survey's actual findings, which are not detailed here.\n\nSource: [ECB - European Central Bank](https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261023~a3d201c97c.en.html)	2026-10-23 08:00:00+00	economy	{EURUSD,DXY}	\N	ECB - European Central Bank	https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261023~a3d201c97c.en.html	33bacda3-c4d5-47b8-8ec4-e885bbd5157f	2026-10-29 20:05:39.937685+00
