dd403e5b-6d45-4e9b-80d2-ea3c88a230e9	EIA releases the Annual Energy Outlook 2026	The Annual Energy Outlook 2026 (AEO2026) explores medium- and long-term alternative futures in the United States through 2050. AEO2026 enables the public to explore a suite of alternative pathways for our energy future depending on assumptions made about markets, technological br	The Annual Energy Outlook 2026 (AEO2026) explores medium- and long-term alternative futures in the United States through 2050. AEO2026 enables the public to explore a suite of alternative pathways for our energy future depending on assumptions made about markets, technological breakthroughs, and policy. It includes a narrative report, as well as the full set of data tables and visualizations, assumptions and methodologies, and detailed descriptions of the 11 cases we ran to explore these alterna\n\nSource: [EIA: Press Releases](/pressroom/releases/press587.php)	2026-04-08 20:00:00+00	markets	{}	\N	EIA: Press Releases	/pressroom/releases/press587.php	33bacda3-c4d5-47b8-8ec4-e885bbd5157f	2026-10-29 20:07:58.747792+00
31fda697-1247-4d4d-850d-d42be0ff4067	Hormuz closure and related production outages are key drivers in EIA's latest forecast	The U.S. Energy Information Administration published its April Short Term Energy Outlook this week, examining the implications of the closure of the Strait of Hormuz.	The U.S. Energy Information Administration published its April Short Term Energy Outlook this week, examining the implications of the closure of the Strait of Hormuz.\n\nSource: [EIA: Press Releases](/pressroom/releases/press586.php)	2026-04-07 17:00:00+00	markets	{}	\N	EIA: Press Releases	/pressroom/releases/press586.php	33bacda3-c4d5-47b8-8ec4-e885bbd5157f	2026-10-29 20:07:58.7478+00
