a5d9aab2-8810-4e2b-91ae-807303657b14	ECB publishes Survey of Professional Forecasters results for Q4 2026	The European Central Bank released the results of its Survey of Professional Forecasters for the fourth quarter of 2026.	The European Central Bank (ECB) has published the results of its Survey of Professional Forecasters (SPF) for the fourth quarter of 2026. The SPF collects professional forecasters' expectations for euro area inflation, GDP growth and unemployment. The release provided here contains no specific figures.\n\nThe survey is closely watched as a gauge of private-sector inflation expectations and their anchoring relative to the ECB's target. Depending on its content, it could influence market pricing of the ECB policy path, with possible spillovers to euro area rates and EURUSD. Higher-than-expected inflation expectations would likely be read as hawkish and supportive of the euro. Softer expectations could reinforce bets on easier policy. Any direct impact is likely to be modest, since the SPF is one input among several for policymakers.\n\nSource: [ECB - European Central Bank](https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261030~e92c3c838c.en.html)	2026-10-30 09:00:00+00	economy	{EURUSD}	\N	ECB - European Central Bank	https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/pr/date/2026/html/ecb.pr261030~e92c3c838c.en.html	9003811b-82a4-4859-bca6-2197a674376a	2026-10-30 09:50:25.835045+00
