bdef5177-a321-44a1-b1e9-2d7a6ee7b284	sig_mn_985596b93b	promote	A loss of momentum in Dubai's key source market for property buyers and tourists could cut real-estate fee and tourism receipts by roughly AED 0.1–0.2bn.	-0.15	India is a leading source of visitors to Dubai, of foreign property buyers and of bilateral non-oil trade. Slower Indian growth and income momentum weakens the RETXN channel first: softer Indian demand for Dubai property means lower DLD transfer fees (4%). It also dents the TOUR channel through fewer leisure and MICE trips and lower hotel-linked fees and Tourism Dirham receipts, with a smaller NOGDP drag via re-export volumes. The estimate is low-confidence and sits near the materiality threshold. It assumes a 3–5% fall in Indian-sourced property volumes plus a minor tourism softening; the poll signals cyclical moderation, not a shock.	- Add an India-demand sensitivity line to the 2027 budget revenue scenarios, stress-testing DLD fees for a 5–10% drop in Indian-buyer volumes.\n- Ask DLD for monthly transaction data by buyer nationality, with an alert if the Indian share falls more than 15% year on year for two consecutive months.\n- Coordinate with DET to shift promotional spend towards less-correlated source markets (GCC, China, Europe) if Indian arrivals slow.\n- Do not use one-off concessions on Indian-buyer fees unless volumes fall well beyond baseline.	- Reuters poll, India growth losing momentum: [Google News/Reuters](https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxNcmFVMDBMZENmZVZuQmM5d0ZOQXhJc01hUzdwc0tMYnR2TXdmVXIyX1lQbXA4Z3FmalNNemVQSlFNX1JDVkZCVkMtNkx4LTBLeWNVemx0SERUZ05pV2dXeUNGaG11b0FhQ3R0ODZnU08zMU5lM3pPcGxnVFJlcUlNQU5ZYkJoQWlYUkZxUE1XZDhic05nM2lTYS14NnZ6NEZZcmJHdU5pSXpZZTZTYUYxcVEtcjBjNi1rVEFPekNn?oc=5)\n- India has ranked among Dubai's top source markets for overnight visitors (Dubai DET data) and among the top foreign nationalities buying Dubai property (DLD data, as reported by Reuters and Bloomberg).\n- The UAE–India CEPA (2022) deepened bilateral trade linkages, increasing Dubai's exposure to the Indian cycle.	claude-opus-5-5	2026-10-29 20:11:48.198
