fe7c9a7c-d455-4422-930d-d6cc401c80cd	sig_mn_d0e2479027	promote	A Chinese wealth shock transmits to Dubai via property buyers, visitors and oil demand, with a plausible impact at or above the AED 0.1bn threshold.	-0.15	A multi-trillion equity drawdown in China erodes household and HNWI wealth, a growing source of Dubai property buyers and long-haul visitors, which pressures DLD transfer fees (RETXN) and tourism-linked fees (TOUR). A risk-off China also signals softer crude demand, weighing on Brent (BRENT) and Dubai's modest oil revenue line. The estimate is low-confidence because only the headline is available; the base case is a 10–20% dip in China-sourced property and tourism fee flows in 2027.	- Instruct DLD to report monthly transaction value by buyer nationality, with a trigger review if China-origin volume falls more than 15% year on year.\n- Rebase the 2027 Brent assumption about $3/bbl lower in the budget stress case.\n- With DET, redirect China-market promotion spend towards India and GCC source markets if Chinese arrivals undershoot the Q1 2027 target.\n- Keep fee rates unchanged and avoid pro-cyclical cuts until the data confirm the drop.	- Source: [The Guardian, 27 Oct 2026](https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/27/chinese-markets-lose-trillions-ai-race-beijing)\n- Analogue: the 2015–16 China equity crash and yuan devaluation coincided with Brent falling below $30/bbl in early 2016 (EIA, IMF WEO 2016).\n- China is a top-10 source market for Dubai visitors (Dubai DET annual statistics); real-estate fee sensitivity is per Dubai DOF budget disclosures.	claude-opus-5-5	2026-10-29 20:32:57.578
