sig_mn_9a3b39d776	Commodity Markets Outlook -- October 2025 - World Bank Group	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxOT2owVzNFa212dzBNemlkVVlvZnJMcDhBZS0wNWxpVkFNV2dhY25kYUQ4SDJXQ1hGU2lzeHlrazVxQlBEbWdGYk1hME1vRlAxV3k0dHFQSUljVG5yZ3hDYTlvNnJPMEFsaHdoYXNRaHNsTzRwakR4dExlZGtVUXRiajNnSlJBVXdTOThkMkhFOEc1dnBVbjFZ?oc=5	"site:worldbank.org (outlook OR forecast OR commodity OR "Middle East" OR Gulf)" - Google News	2025-10-17 07:00:00	MACRO	CANDIDATE	[rashid · model=claude-opus-5-5] The October 2025 Commodity Markets Outlook extends the World Bank's softer energy-price path into 2026, driven by an oil supply surplus as OPEC+ unwinds cuts and global demand growth slows. BRENT channel: Dubai's direct hydrocarbon receipts are a modest share of revenue (indicatively ~5%, i.e. a few AED bn), so a sustained ~USD 8–10/bbl shortfall versus budget assumptions implies roughly AED 0.3–0.4bn of lost oil revenue in 2027. A smaller indirect drag comes through NOGDP and PMI, as weaker GCC liquidity dampens regional trade, property demand and fee-generating activity. Combined central estimate: about AED -0.5bn. The feed does not include the report's figures, so this rests on directional channels and the price levels should be checked against the source.	-0.5	0	\N	\N	0.85	2	\N	\N	2026-10-29 20:27:45.491	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	6e2f716e-5a6b-4e4d-bcc3-c4b9f42edee2	Agent Rashid
sig_mn_64af702f4a	Commodity Markets Outlook (April 2025) - World Bank Group	https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxPb2VjV21TNFEtb0E0R2dqVjVaSDUzS0d0anNuQnItU1ZucWtQX3RVcnR3N3Awdkpwa0xwVUwxaGt3TjI3M3Q1QU5FeTI3bkw3MENGdXBCVDZuT3NpRTdzNmt3UWNuaHloUHFVdDlZUWNIZWtnUHRKcGQ2SWRFbHRUbjZQQlQzZkJBa1ZVelNFTWJZdWwteTJ6X3F0bnNfX2JYM2JZMnJwalJtd1RlTW9HNTNVYmMxZ19z?oc=5	"site:worldbank.org (outlook OR forecast OR commodity OR "Middle East" OR Gulf)" - Google News	2025-04-29 07:00:00	MACRO	CANDIDATE	[rashid · model=claude-opus-5-5] The World Bank's April 2025 outlook cuts its Brent path to about $64/bbl in 2025 and $60/bbl in 2026, against an average of about $81 in 2024. That is a fall of roughly 25%, which flows directly into Dubai's oil and hydrocarbon-linked receipts (BRENT channel). There are smaller second-round effects through weaker GCC liquidity, slower re-export and trade volumes (DXY/NOGDP channel) and softer property demand from regional buyers (RETXN channel). Oil is a modest share of Dubai revenue, so the hit is material but contained. Our working estimate for 2027 is about AED -0.9bn versus a budget built on $70–75 oil.	-0.9	0	\N	\N	0.85	2	\N	\N	2026-10-29 20:28:42.073	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	84f20ecb-c12c-4310-8b77-02fc9ff0876a	Agent Rashid
